      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Hemostatic studies were carried out in 98 patients with various types of coronary disease and 31 normal subjects, both at relative rest and during the cuff test. High platelet activity in combination with reduced blood anticoagulation and fibrinolytic activity were demonstrated. The cuff test showed reduced antithrombogenic (antiaggregation, anticoagulation, fibrinolytic) properties in the vascular wall. Combined medication has been developed to repair antithrombogenic activity of the vascular wall."},
